From 256c9b70335c4abe20b53f546fa4d18426193cea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Lintermann <rl@karo-electronics.de>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:29:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] board: karo: add support for the QS95-5610 i.MX95 module

Add support for the Ka-Ro electronics QS95-5610 solder-in module with
an NXP i.MX95 SoC, together with the QSBASE95 baseboard:

- board code with SPL, board specific imx_get_mac_from_fuse(),
  environment handling (env location selection, MAC address from
  fuse/env) and FDT fixups in board/karo/
- device trees for the module and for the module on the QSBASE95
  baseboard
- defconfigs for the standard image, a manufacturing image for use
  with UUU/MfGTool (no environment, no autoboot delay) and a variant
  using only the built-in environment
- TARGET_KARO_IMX95 target and Kconfig wiring

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [karo-specific]
Signed-off-by: Robin Lintermann <rl@karo-electronics.de>

Generated by Mistral Vibe.
Co-Authored-By: Mistral Vibe <vibe@mistral.ai>
